    "raw": "Given:\n- 2 chapters of the textbook, each requiring 3 hours of study.\n- 4 worksheets, each requiring 1.5 hours of study.\n- They plan to study no more than 4 hours each day.\n- They take a 10-minute break every hour.\n- They also take 3 10-minute snack breaks each day.\n- They have 30 minutes for lunch each day.\n\nFirst, calculate the total study time needed:\n- For the chapters: \\(2 \\times 3 = 6\\) hours.\n- For the worksheets: \\(4 \\times 1.5 = 6\\) hours.\n- Total study time: \\(6 + 6 = 12\\) hours.\n\nNext, calculate the effective study time per day, considering breaks and lunch:\n- They take a 10-minute break every hour, so for 4 hours of study, they take \\(4 \\times 10 = 40\\) minutes in breaks.\n- They also take 3 10-minute snack breaks each day, which is \\(3 \\times 10 = 30\\) minutes.\n- They have 30 minutes for lunch.\n- Total time not available for studying per day: \\(40 + 30 + 30 = 100\\) minutes or \\(1 \\frac{2}{3}\\) hours.\n\nThus, the effective study time per day is:\n- \\(4 - 1 \\frac{2}{3} = 2 \\frac{1}{3}\\) hours or \\(2.33\\) hours.\n\nNow, calculate the number of days needed to study 12 hours:\n- \\(12 \\div 2.33 \\approx 5.14\\).\n\nSince they can't study a fraction of a day, they need to round up to the next whole number, which is 6 days.\n\nFINAL: 6",
